# Example environment for the live integration/contract tests.
# Copy to `.env` and fill in your own values. NEVER commit the real `.env`
# (it is git-ignored).
#
# `.env` is loaded automatically by the live tiers — just run:
#   npm run test:integration
#   npm run test:contract
# (`test/setup-env.cjs` loads it; the unit tier deliberately does not.) In CI the
# same variables come from GitHub secrets, which take precedence over any `.env`.
#
# Quote any value containing spaces or newlines — notably the Custody signing
# key below. `\n` inside double quotes is expanded, so a PEM can stay on one
# line. (An unquoted PEM also breaks `source .env`, if you load it that way.)
#
# All live tests are gated: each suite SKIPS when its variables are absent, so
# `npm test` (unit) and the offline gate pass with none of these set.

# ─── XRPL network (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The WebSocket endpoint the live tier runs against. Defaults to the public
# Testnet when unset; override to point at another network (e.g. a devnet).
# XRPL_TESTNET_WS=wss://s.altnet.rippletest.net:51233

# ─── IOU integration tests ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two funded Testnet accounts (issuer + hot wallet). Create with
# Account.create(), fund via the faucet. Seeds are secrets — do not commit.
XRPL_ISSUER_SEED=
XRPL_HOT_WALLET_SEED=

# ─── Palisade sandbox contract tests ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Enables test/contract/palisade.contract.test.ts (skips if any required var is
# blank). See the file header for how each maps to the sandbox UI.
PALISADE_BASE_URL=https://api.sandbox.palisade.co
# Palisade scopes one permission set per credential, so a full setup needs two:
# a wallet-read credential (account discovery) and a transactions one (signing).
PALISADE_WALLETS_CLIENT_ID=
PALISADE_WALLETS_CLIENT_SECRET=
PALISADE_TX_CLIENT_ID=
PALISADE_TX_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional: a credential scoped to the Palisade `Policies` permission set, for
# tag-based routing on `palisade.api` (see examples/13). Leave blank to skip.
PALISADE_POLICY_CLIENT_ID=
PALISADE_POLICY_CLIENT_SECRET=
PALISADE_VAULT_ID=
PALISADE_WALLET_ID=
# A second org wallet's r-address, used as the Payment destination (Palisade's
# native transfer only accepts destinations it knows). When unset, the Payment
# test is skipped.
PALISADE_DEST_ADDRESS=
# A second org wallet's r-address used as the IOU hot wallet (holder) in the
# example 06 snippet. Must be a Palisade wallet that can sign a TrustSet.
PALISADE_HOLDER_ADDRESS=

# ─── AWS KMS contract test (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Enables test/contract/aws-kms.contract.test.ts.
# AWS_KMS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_REGION=

# ─── Ripple Custody v1 (separate product, not the Palisade sandbox) ───────────
# Enables test/contract/ripple-custody.contract.test.ts. All five below are
# required — the suite skips unless every one is set.
# RIPPLE_CUSTODY_GATEWAY_URL=
# The full OAuth token endpoint, not the auth server's base URL. Posting to the
# base URL returns a redirect with no access_token, which surfaces as
# "Custody token response had no access_token".
# RIPPLE_CUSTODY_AUTH_TOKEN_URL=
# PEM private key: literal contents, a path to a `.pem` file, or an AWS Secrets
# Manager secret ARN. Quote literal PEM contents and use \n between lines.
# RIPPLE_CUSTODY_AUTH_SIGNING_KEY=
# RIPPLE_CUSTODY_DOMAIN_ID=
# The primary account's r-address. Note the `_ADDRESS` suffix.
# RIPPLE_CUSTODY_PRIMARY_ADDRESS=
# Optional: defaults to `customer_api` and to the signing key's public half.
# RIPPLE_CUSTODY_AUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# RIPPLE_CUSTODY_AUTH_PUBLIC_KEY=
